-- title:
--   Weil differentials bounded by D versus mod-p cusp functions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$, a nonzero level $N$ with $p \nmid N$, and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$; let $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ be the subfield $K(j(q), j(q^N))$ of $K((q))$ generated by the Laurent series `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`, and write $\bar j$ for `jGeomGen K N`, the element $j(q)$ of $F$. Assume $F/K$ carries the canonical local residue data at every place, has a canonical divisor and principal divisors, that $\Omega_{F/K}$ is nontrivial and is generated at each place $w$ by $d\pi_w$, and that Weil and Kähler theories agree (`WeilKaehlerAgree`: for every $\omega \ne 0$ the functional `weilOfKaehler` attached to $\omega$ is nonzero, lies in the $\Omega$-space of $(\omega)$, and $(\omega)$ dominates every divisor $D$ whose $\Omega$-space contains it). Assume further $d\bar j \ne 0$; integers $m, m' \ge 1$ with $m + m' = (p+1)/2$; an element $h \in F$ whose Laurent expansion is $\theta(j)^{-(p-1)/2}$, where $\theta f = q\,\frac{df}{dq}$ and the exponent is the integer quotient; that every place $w$ is affine geometric (both $\bar j$ and $j(q^N)$ lie in its valuation ring) or satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_w \bar j < 0$; and that $|\operatorname{ord}_w \bar j|$ is nonzero in $K$ whenever $\operatorname{ord}_w \bar j < 0$. Let $D$ be a divisor on $F$ with $D(w) = \mathrm{weightFloor}\,K\,N\,m\,(w) - 1$ at those places $w$ that are supersingular (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in `ssJSet p K`) and whose width `placeWidth N w` divides $m$, and $D(w) = \mathrm{weightFloor}\,K\,N\,m\,(w)$ at all other places. Then for every $f \in F$ with $f \ne 0$, the Weil differential `weilOfKaehler` attached to $f\,d\bar j$ — the functional sending an adele $\alpha$ to $\sum_w \operatorname{Tr}_{K(w)/K}\operatorname{res}_w(\alpha_w \cdot (f\,d\bar j)/d\pi_w)$ — annihilates the adeles bounded by $D$ together with the global elements, i.e. lies in $\mathrm{omegaSpace}\,D$, if and only if the Laurent series of $f h$ satisfies `IsModPCuspFormFn K m'`: $G^6 j^{4m'}(j-1728)^{3m'}$ is integral over $K[j]$ and $G^{2M} j^{m'M+1}(j-1728)^{m'M}$ is integral over $K[j^{-1}]$ for some $M$.
--
--   This is the Kodaira–Spencer identification at the supersingular places: multiplication by the Hasse invariant function $h$ carries the differentials bounded by the weight-$2m$ floor divisor minus the supersingular places of width dividing $m$ onto the mod-$p$ cusp functions of weight $2m'$, $m+m'=(p+1)/2$. It is the dictionary used on the Hecke-equivariant comparison in the weight part of Serre's conjecture, and is invoked in [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit).
